# SlayZone Env Vars — Standalone Hub & Runner

Deployment-relevant vars for standalone (non-supervised) hub + runner, plus every var surfaced by the full 4-cluster deep-dive. Dev/build/e2e/internal vars summarized at bottom.

**Precedence everywhere:** `env var > SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CONFIG file (runner) > ~/.slayzone/config.json > generated/default`

**CWD-anchoring = default-only, NO new knob.** Standalone (non-supervised) hub/runner default `SLAYZONE_HOME_DIR` + `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR` + `SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CREDENTIALS_DIR` to CWD. Relocate = `cd /srv/slayzone && slayzone-hub`.

**`SLAYZONE_HUB_` rename (hub-only vars).** Only vars read EXCLUSIVELY by the hub get the prefix — hub-package blast radius, no app/CLI churn. Shared server/data vars (`DB_PATH`, `STORE_DIR`, `PORT`, `HOST`, `DB_DIR`, `HOME_DIR`) are deliberately NOT renamed (they belong to the shared embedded server run by app+CLI too; renaming breaks supervised). config.json keys unchanged (env rename only).

**Minimize legend** (does the operator hold info the process can't derive at boot?):
- 🟢 **keep** · 🔵 **derive** (optional override) · 🟠 **hide** (subsumed, code stays) · 🔴 **delete**

